<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Masuna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 508</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Masuna was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> king in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>, named in an inscription of 508 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altava">Altava</a> as king of the peoples of the Moors and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>. He is probably the Massonas whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/procopius">Procopius</a> describes as an ally of the Byzantine general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> against other Berber rulers in 535. His kingdom is one of the best-attested successor states of Roman Mauretania.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/masuna.jpg" alt="Masuna" width="320" height="123" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inscription_that_refers_to_king_Masuna.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
